  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Mia walk to the pond. Tom and Ben play badminton. Tom hits it, and Ben runs. Ben hits it, too. It flies and flies. \"Look at me!\" says Ben. Tom throws a red ball to Pip. Pip jumps!",
      "\"Look, a frog!\" says Lily. The frog is green and small. It sits next to the water. Mia walks to the frog. \"Hello, frog,\" she says. The frog jumps, and jumps again! Pip runs to the frog. \"Can Pip catch it?\" asks Mia. \"Woof, woof!\" says Pip. Pip hits his red ball with his nose.",
      "The red ball goes in the pond. Then the frog jumps on it! What does the frog do? The frog sits on the red ball. It can swim, and it can sit. Pip stops and looks. Tom and Ben clap their hands. \"The frog likes the ball,\" says Tom. Mia smiles. \"Sit on it, frog,\" says Lily. The frog is happy now."
    ],
    "summary": "Lily and Mia walk to the pond, where Tom and Ben play badminton. A frog jumps, Pip runs, and the red ball goes in the water with the frog on it.",
